This directory holds the first-party source-connector plugin binaries embedded
into the single control-plane artifact (CB-1 transport B, see ../embed.go).

It is populated by `task build:connectors`, which compiles each first-party
SOURCE connector (e.g. connectors/claude/cmd/claude-source) to a standalone
binary here for the build's target platform. Those binaries are NOT committed
(they are build artifacts, and platform-specific); only this placeholder is, so
the //go:embed pattern stays valid on a connector-less `go build`/`go test`.

At runtime the engine extracts a needed binary to a private temp dir and launches
it as an isolated go-plugin subprocess (AutoMTLS), so a connector's dependency
tree never links into the core. When a configured plugin source has no embedded
binary, the composition root warns and skips it — never a silent no-op.
